.TH LOD.QOS_PRIO_FREE 4 2026-09-29 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
lod.qos_prio_free, lod.mdt_qos_prio_free \- weight of target free space
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param lod." FSNAME "*.qos_prio_free"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param lod." FSNAME "*.qos_prio_free=" PERCENT
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param lod." FSNAME "*.mdt_qos_prio_free"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param lod." FSNAME "*.mdt_qos_prio_free=" PERCENT
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Perms
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-MDT
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present on MDS nodes
.TP
.B Default
.br
.RB lod.*.qos_prio_free= 90%
.br
.RB lod.*.mdt_qos_prio_free= 90%
.TP
.B Valid Range
.br
.RB lod.*.qos_prio_free= 0%
.br
.RB lod.*.qos_prio_free= 100%
.br
.RB lod.*.mdt_qos_prio_free= 0%
.br
.RB lod.*.mdt_qos_prio_free= 100%
.SH DESCRIPTION
When the free space of the targets differs by more than
.BR lod.qos_threshold_rr (4),
the MDS allocates new objects by the free space of each target.
.B qos_prio_free
controls how strongly the free space of the OSTs is followed, and
.B mdt_qos_prio_free
that of the MDTs for the stripes of new striped directories.
.PP
OST objects are allocated in round-robin order, but each OST is used in
proportion to its weight, which is its free space.
.B qos_prio_free
moves the weight of each OST with more free space than the average down
toward the average weight of all of them, by
.RI "(100% - " PERCENT )
of the difference.
With 100% the OSTs are used in proportion to their free space, and with
0% the OSTs with more than the average free space are used equally, as
with round-robin allocation.
The weight of an OST with less than the average free space is not
changed, so fuller OSTs are always used less often.
An OST gets at most one stripe of each file, so the weight of an OST
with much more free space than the others is limited to its share of
the file stripe count.
.PP
MDTs are chosen at random, with a weight of their free space and free
inodes, less a penalty for each recently used MDT and MDS, which decays
over time.
.B mdt_qos_prio_free
is the priority of the free space in the weight compared to the
penalties, which spread new directories over MDTs that have not been
used recently.
.PP
The
.B %
sign is optional when setting the value, which is kept in 1/256 steps.
Setting it also resets the penalties.
.SH EXAMPLES
Allocate OST objects in proportion to the free space of the OSTs on all
MDTs of the
.B testfs
filesystem:
.EX
.RB "mds# " "lctl set_param lod.testfs-*.qos_prio_free=100"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B qos_prio_free
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.4.0, and
.B mdt_qos_prio_free
since release 2.13.0.
Before that it was
.BR lov.qos_prio_free ,
since release 1.8.0.
OST allocation is weighted round-robin since release 2.18.0.
